Z||000050||fierohoho||07-15-2001||01:08 PM||||Had a great time except we lost you guys at the light in St Paul and didn't know where you went.<P>Jaei Sun and Rick and I ended up making one pass with all the hotrods and went to Arby's, they decided to leave so my buddy Jeff and I got some food and sat on the sidewalk to watch the cars, lots of cool cars.<P>The time at Calhoun was great, got to meet Tina and Rick, even had some club members show.<P>Lots of head turning when we bailed to go to St.Paul, did anyone not squeel their tires?<P>We have got to do this again, no car show just cars and car chat. <P>Thanks for comming everyone it was a blast.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||8
Z||000051||Tina||07-15-2001||06:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierohoho:<BR><B>Had a great time except we lost you guys at the light in St Paul and didn't know where you went.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Yep, that was to bad. <BR>I had a bad feeling it was going to happen.<BR>A couple of cell #'s would of been handy to have.<BR>I pretty much had to stay behind Standard though,since I had no clue where Porky's was.<P>(Orange light,or not)<BR>Well exept for the time,St.Paul's finest pulled right behind him.We thought he was toast for sure  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Tina<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000052||elfiero||07-15-2001||08:01 PM||||I just sent standard the pics so they should<BR>be posted soon.I thought there was some great<BR>people and even better cars there!Don'tcha<BR>wish all fiero get-togethers were that much<BR>fun???we will have to figure out somthing<BR>else to do B-4 fall,nothing major,just get<BR>together for the heck of it!||||reg||6
Z||000053||fierohoho||07-15-2001||08:47 PM||||Still thinking about the meet.<P>I would also like to say sorry to Jaei Sun for all the stale yellow lights I went through trying to keep up, (he was last in line behind me) and really sorry for all those stale red lights I went through trying to keep up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <P>I can't believe I went through some of them let alone when he went through some behind me.<P>You are either a good driver or quite insane, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> it was fun.<P>I think we need to practice more so we get this get-together right.<P><BR>Elfiero is right, we need to do this again.<P>How about Saturday, August 11th, this time we meet at a different place with plenty of exposure.<P>Any suggestions or thoughts?<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000054||Jaei Sun||07-15-2001||09:57 PM||||Well if it's one area I know is uptown.<P>When I got stuck at the reds on lake St. I just (safely) went to the side streets where there are no stop lights.  I could do the speed limit on those back streets and keep up with the rest.  <P>As for the lights, yellows in that area stay yellow a little longer than the ones where I live.  As for the driving, I'm planning on Auto-xing when I get some better suspension.<P>As for more meetings I couldn't agree more!  I started making a site with a listing of more gatherings, those who want to attend can come whenever they want to.  I agree with the more exposure for sure!<P>Next time there is a cruse everyone should have directions of the path so if some get stuck behind lights.<P>Another idea for a meeting place is Wagner's Drive In, off hwy 7 St. Louis Park.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://home.mn.rr.com/fierojaei/trans_fiero_sig2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Jaei Sun (edited 07-15-2001).]||||reg||1
